From: Joel Gerber <Jitsusama@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Hold the JavaScript heap's pages once

Linux's JavaScript heap was reserved as a private mapping of a memfd,
which named it in the process's maps. Each page the heap wrote was a
private copy of the memfd's own page, which the kernel made in the
memfd as the page was first written and kept until the heap was
unmapped, so every page of the heap was held twice, and decommitting a
chunk let go of only its copy: a shell holding 132 MB of heap held
159 MB more of memfd pages unmapped. The heap is now anonymous memory,
so each page is held once and decommitting lets it go, and a first
write is the cheapest of the three: 128 MB took 33 to 41 ms against
55 to 78 from a private memfd and 39 to 53 from a shared one. The name
is given to the mapping instead, which the kernel keeps only when built
to name anonymous memory. Every other mapping is as it was.

---
--- a/src/3rdparty/masm/wtf/OSAllocatorPosix.cpp
+++ b/src/3rdparty/masm/wtf/OSAllocatorPosix.cpp
@@ -40,6 +40,11 @@
 #if OS(LINUX)
 #include <sys/syscall.h>
 #include <linux/limits.h>
+#include <sys/prctl.h>
+#ifndef PR_SET_VMA
+#define PR_SET_VMA 0x53564d41
+#define PR_SET_VMA_ANON_NAME 0
+#endif
 #ifndef MFD_CLOEXEC
 #define MFD_CLOEXEC         0x0001U
 #endif
@@ -109,12 +114,22 @@
 #elif OS(LINUX)
     UNUSED_PARAM(writable);
     UNUSED_PARAM(executable);
-    int fd = memfdForUsage(bytes, usage);
+    // The JavaScript heap is anonymous memory, so each page it writes is
+    // held once. Mapped private from a memfd, each written page was a copy
+    // of the memfd's own, which the kernel made as the page was first
+    // written and kept until the heap was unmapped, so the heap was held
+    // twice, and decommitting a chunk let go of only its copy. The name
+    // the memfd gave it is given to the mapping instead, where the kernel
+    // can name anonymous memory.
+    const bool heap = usage == OSAllocator::JSGCHeapPages;
+    int fd = heap ? -1 : memfdForUsage(bytes, usage);
 
     void* result = mmap(0, bytes, PROT_NONE, MAP_NORESERVE | MAP_PRIVATE |
                         (fd == -1 ? MAP_ANON : 0), fd, 0);
     if (result == MAP_FAILED)
         CRASH();
+    if (heap)
+        prctl(PR_SET_VMA, PR_SET_VMA_ANON_NAME, result, bytes, "JSGCHeap:QtQml");
 
     if (fd != -1)
         close(fd);
